[
  {
    "sha": "09d515d7e30ab5e668d83269d33a723968e63a28",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoKkgNoAKDA5ZDUxNWQ3ZTMwYWI1ZTY2OGQ4MzI2OWQzM2E3MjM5NjhlNjNhMjg",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "tbrasselle",
        "email": "tbrasselle@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-22T15:56:35Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "tbrasselle",
        "email": "tbrasselle@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-22T15:56:35Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(multiaxis): swing the rotaries before the approach descent\n\nThe five-axis approach set the first station pose on the modal\nbuilder and then pushed the Plunge to first contact, so the rotary\nswing rode the descend. The approach now states the pose as its own\nzero-travel rapid (a standstill rotary index on the hop plane, the\ntip held) before the plunge, in contour_curve and in the stamp emit\nloop for every posed kind. The builder keeps a zero-travel move whose\npose changed and the post solves it as a pure rotary reorientation,\nso the swing always commands. Intermediate cut moves keep the modal\ntilt law.\n\nThe law tests that read rapids and ball centres now read the\nswing-free stream (no_swings/sans_swings helpers); a decision record\nsits in docs/decisions/3414-approach-rotary-order.md.\n\nFixes #3414",
      "tree": {
