  {
    "sha": "acb9d8bc0ebe3a86e2a3ab44f5ffff23c5bb2fde",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoKkgNoAKGFjYjlkOGJjMGViZTNhODZlMmEzYWI0NGY1ZmZmZjIzYzViYjJmZGU",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "tbrasselle",
        "email": "tbrasselle@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-23T04:14:50Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "tbrasselle",
        "email": "tbrasselle@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-23T04:14:50Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(multiaxis): swing the rotaries upright before an upright approach\n\nThe #3414 standstill swing ran only in the leaned arm of the stamp.\nBoth upright arms (the arc arm and the linear arm) stated an upright\npose directly on an air-to-cut move, so a rapid that travelled under\na lean handed the descent a 90-degree rotary turn: on multiaxis_rough\nover the slab with a boss, move 261 turned back to upright while it\nreached the part.\n\nBoth upright arms now emit the same zero-travel rapid when they are\nreached out of air (in_air), the move is not a Rapid, and a held pose\nexists and differs from the upright one. An opening upright move from\nheld_pose == None states the upright home as its own (#3300) and\nswings nothing; a pose that already matches drops in the builder, byte\nfor byte as before. The ball only rises through the swing, so nothing\nnew is swept.\n\nPinned two ways: the_approach_rotates_before_it_descends now runs\nno_pose_change_rides_the_air_to_cut_move over multiaxis_rough\n(slab_with_boss) and contour5d, red at the reviewer's exact move 261\nwithout the linear arm's swing; and the new stamp unit test\nan_upright_arc_out_of_air_swings_at_a_standstill_first is red without\nthe arc arm's swing. The decision record cites onRapid and tilt()\nfor the posted rotary index, not the g93 feed branch.\n\nRefs #3414",
