      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "tbrasselle",
        "email": "tbrasselle@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-23T04:36:11Z"
      },
      "message": "test: keep the opening upright statement out of the swing filters\n\nThe merged #3300 law states the upright home on the opening move. The\napp's rough ladder opens with a zero-travel Rapid (the plan's own first\nmove states no travel), so the stamp's opening statement is a\nzero-travel Rapid with axis Some([0, 0, 1]). The no_swings and\nsans_swings filters read it as a rotary index - a zero-travel Rapid\nwhose axis changes off no held pose - and stripped it, which desynced\nthe plain-vs-posed pairing in multiaxis_rough_peels_the_same_ladder_\nand_poses_its_walls (the ball moved at 0).\n\nA swing is a zero-travel rapid whose axis CHANGED; an opening upright\nstatement from held_pose == None is the home the path inherits,\ncommanded as zero angles, and no rotation happens. All three filter\ncopies (app no_swings, motion sans_swings x2) now keep it; a leaned\nopening from no held pose still counts as a swing.\n\nRefs #3414",
